    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92758360_c61d3fba",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T07:19:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, if I have made you feel confused. The existence of \u0027framework\u0027 and \u0027ext\u0027 in the whitelist made me to think that this implementation doesn\u0027t distinguish dependency that will be part of the app and those won\u0027t.\n\nMy proposal is doing the two checks that I presented just above.\n\n\u003e 1) everything that are \"part\" of an app (or an apex) should have min_sdk_version: 29.\n\u003e 2) all the external dependencies (things that are not part of the app or apex) should be satisfied by SDK 29.\n\nAbove is about \u0027what\u0027, not \u0027how\u0027 though. \n\nAs for \"how\", I suggest implementing this by traversing the graph from the root node (app); you gather all dependencies that becomes part of the app. It includes static java dependencies and static/dynamic native dependencies except for the libraries providing stub. Then you make sure that they all satisfy msv \u003c\u003d 29 and don\u0027t have any extra dynamic java dependency other than SDK stubs.\n\n\u003e checking every library dozen of times (death by thousand cuts)\n\nYes, for some of the commonly used libraries, we will be running the check multiple times (per app). However, I believe build performance less important than making the check correct. Also, given that we only have a few Mainline module apks, I don\u0027t think the performance hit is significant. Nevertheless, if there is any way to improve the performance while keeping the check correct, I am on it.",
      "parentUuid": "1b603939_9e80fd06",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 158,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 159,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "52ab56b583cc86a6771eb8fa6d8afa21b6fbb08b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "520dcb78_0a2aa39d",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T14:42:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we are speaking past each other somewhere here... :-) Let me know if you want to chat f2f.\n\nIt does recognizes stubs. There is an if check for stubs to ignore them. It does still check any other non-static-libs for compliance though. For example, annotation jars and unsupportedappusage that go in libs and don\u0027t end up in the binary (ideally, unless annotation has runtime retention). Note that \"framework\" is not a stub per se; also it doesn\u0027t go into any mainline modules. It was just a side-effect, because the check was implmenented for all java modules.\n\nFor your points:\n1) This is something that Jooyung is doing for Apexes in aosp/1287253. Jooyung, you also mentioned that you are going to cover APKS as well, since you are fixing native code there as well. With that we are guaranteed with msv of a binary \u003c\u003d msv of a library.\n2) This cannot really happen for java. In java, sdk_version is always \"current\" if the library is under active development (e.g. networkstack). So, we are going to guarantee that it compiles against a stable SDK separately via checkLintType.\n\nSo, external deps are not really covered for minSdkVersion by your proposal. Which may be okay if we guarantee they are behind a stable interface (since I assume most mainline modules aren\u0027t doing anything funky with external deps). Eventually we do want a static analysis on the boundaries to enforce min_sdk_version requirements then. (Or we submit this change and have partial enforcement at build time).\n\ntl;dr we need stable sdk check for java (aosp/1285396), Jooyung is working on adding binary level min_sdk_version check for transitive deps (both for apex and apk). Both of these should cover near-term requirements, but we need something more robust (lint) going forward, since we should allow for java to depend on something with higher min_sdk_version.",
      "parentUuid": "92758360_c61d3fba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 158,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 159,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "52ab56b583cc86a6771eb8fa6d8afa21b6fbb08b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
